\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Rewrite completeness over a real-closed field}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Gao, Shaikh, and Kissinger \citek{gao2026graphical}, in
the conclusion, leave open the construction of graphical
algebraic geometry over the reals. For a real-closed field,
the generators can express an inequality #{g(x)\ge 0}. They
use complete for a complete set of rewrite rules, and they
say that finding those rules may be difficult and will
involve the Positivstellensätze.}
